This boundary contains backend applications and reusable backend libraries.
Later capability pieces own the exact files placed beneath these roots.

## Directory map

- Boundary root: `{{backend.root}}`
- Runnable service or worker packages: `{{backend.appsRoot}}/`
- Reusable backend libraries: `{{backend.libsRoot}}/`

Applications own runtime composition, entry points, and application-specific
adapters. Libraries hold reusable domain, contract, data-access, and utility
boundaries. Domain code should not depend directly on infrastructure adapters.
Generated artifacts are outputs, not maintained source, and must remain
distinguishable from both application and library code.

This structure does not select a framework, transport, database, deployment
system, build tool, or test runner.
